# Independent site rc.5 adoption review

Result: no concrete adoption blocker found in the frozen candidate. This is an
independent agent's bounded source and runtime review, not human practitioner
sign-off, complete numerical certification, a full site gate receipt, or a
publication/deployment/adoption claim.

## Identity and execution

The review froze twelve source inputs from the working tree whose HEAD was
`d63773a3be2b4d40ff28a1075b9aaa9cb6c10793`. `snapshot.json` records each SHA-256;
`source.patch` records the tracked dirty diff. A fresh isolated directory was
created at `/private/tmp/zodiacs-platform-rc5-independent-review`. No prior scratch
results were reused as execution evidence. The package archives were copied and
extracted into separate rc.1 and rc.5 module trees; the exact installed Astronomy
Engine 2.1.19 dependency and esbuild tooling were copied without install scripts
or network. Root site files were not edited by this reviewer.

`probe.mjs` executed successfully against both frozen installed packages on:

- Node 22.23.2, ICU 78.2, tzdata 2026a: 291 checks passed.
- Node 24.19.0, ICU 78.3, tzdata 2026b: 291 checks passed.

See `probe-node22.log`, `probe-node24.log`, `result-node22.json`, and
`result-node24.json`. Each check name is retained. The counts are assertion
groups rather than a count of individual assertions. These executions do not
rerun or relabel the author's 247 checks.

## Compatibility and boundaries

The harness bundles the actual unchanged site `full.ts`, `houses.ts`,
`aspects.ts`, and `types.ts` separately against each extracted package. It does
not replace the adapter with a modeled projection.

- 128 natal calculations compare every existing site Chart field, excluding only
  top-level `engineVersion`; a further five exercise unknown time, missing
  location, LMT, DST fold, and DST gap flags. Caller input object identity is
  retained in the regular matrix. Eight epochs cover years 0004, 0099, 1600,
  1900, 2000, 2024, 2026 and 2199. Eight locations include the equator, northern
  and southern mid-latitudes, the 66-degree threshold, just beyond it, both
  polar hemispheres, and a near-pole control. Both house requests are tested.
- Eight body/aspect sets and 192 single-body longitude/speed values agree exactly.
- 72 direct house configurations agree exactly across nine latitudes, four
  sidereal times and both requested systems.
- Public/internal/site export names, function arities and non-version constants
  are unchanged. Separate browser dependency graphs confirm receipt and geo
  remain optional, the site math graph remains free of the astronomical
  ephemeris, and no tested entry imports the ownership SDK. `graphs.json`
  retains the actual esbuild module inputs.
- 85 hostile JSON-representable metadata variations are rejected: missing and
  null fields, malformed identities, query/fragment suffixes,
  mutable commit refs, newline tricks, path traversal, unexpected keys and
  inconsistent carrier paths. The original candidate and the explicitly
  supported owned-site artifact carrier pass. This local metadata validator
  checks canonical claims; it does not authenticate remote source commits.
- Full public Chart receipts round-trip and replay correctly for known and
  unknown 08:30 UTC instants with polar requested Placidus, retaining exact
  source ISO spelling and requested versus actual houses. The receipt replay
  intentionally emits an explicit empty input flag array when it was omitted
  from the original input; the probe declares that single representational
  normalization explicitly.

`charts.json` records the matrix inputs, actual houses/flags and paired result
hashes. Exact parity is not independent astronomical accuracy. No numerical
fixture, tolerance or original site expected value was altered.

Two limits remain explicit. The compact site body records omit the full public
Chart's sign/degree fields, so direct receipt construction from that compact
Chart correctly throws; this pin does not implement receipt storage or an
account migration. Also, the site still calls the internal engine boundary:
rc.5 public-input validation does not automatically harden internal callers.

