## Failed harness attempts retained

`initial-harness-cjs-resolution.log` records the first harness attempting
CommonJS `require.resolve` on an ESM-only import export. It failed before adapter
execution. The resolver now follows each frozen package's explicit `import`
export. The failed attempt used the shell's Node 26.4.0; successful acceptance
uses the explicit Node 22/24 binaries above.

`initial-receipt-expectation.log` records a harness expectation that omitted the
specified `houses.absenceReason` field. The expected full record was corrected
from the packed declared schema to include `null` or `unknown-time`; no candidate
code was changed. Both corrected runtimes pass. These are harness failures,
not concealed candidate passes.

Full site tests, build, browser layout checks, refreshed daily/capture evidence,
CI and preview delivery remain the accountable integrator's separate work.

